# NOT EXECUTABLE - parked design, per the specifier's BL-233 rule. No
# *.feature glob and no step handler picks this up. It exists so the
# scenarios cut from BL-586's live contract are preserved rather than lost.
#
# Why these are parked and not minted:
#
# 1. Multi-writer detection (was BL-586 scenario 05). BL-586's own
#    description concedes the mechanism is "root mechanism unproven (writes
#    interleaved, no audit trail)", and the 2026-08-21 intake found "not an
#    obvious dual-stack today". A fix for an unreproduced race is a spike,
#    not a gateable slice (INVEST: Estimable, Testable). Its one gateable
#    assertion - "the board does not post into a topic the surviving state
#    cannot validate" - is not deferred at all: it is exactly what BL-586
#    scenario 01 now gates, on every resolve, regardless of which writer won.
#
# 2. Posting noise (was BL-586 scenario 06, plus the delete+repost and
#    chat-level pin fan-out). The human's 2026-08-21 intake gives a
#    CONDITIONAL directive on this, quoted verbatim in BL-586's YAML:
#    "Do not treat pin-spam as a separate mint unless BL-586's identity fix
#    leaves the notification storm intact - then a follow-up slice: stop
#    chat-level pin fan-out / stop delete+repost notifying every tick."
#    The condition is evaluated AFTER BL-586 lands. BL-586's YAML carries
#    the check as a named post-landing step so it cannot be forgotten.

Feature: pipeline board posting is quiet and its identity survives concurrent writers

  # BL-586-deferred concurrent-writers-log-loudly-05
  Scenario: two concurrent writers of board identity produce a loud log naming both
    Given two front-desk stacks are running concurrently and both write pipeline-board identity
    When their writes conflict
    Then a loud log line names both stack identities and both topic ids

  # BL-586-deferred link-previews-disabled-06
  Scenario: board messages send with link previews disabled
    Given a board message body contains a GitHub link
    When the board sends that message
    Then the message is sent with link previews disabled

  # BL-586-deferred no-chat-level-pin-fan-out-07
  Scenario: a board repost does not emit a chat-level pin service message
    Given the board has already pinned its current message
    When a content change causes the board to repost
    Then no chat-level pin service message is emitted into another topic
